A||||7||BAM-BAM||How do I remove the side moulding?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||03:44 PM|||| Need to know how to remove the side moulding on my 85GT. I may want to change over to the round. LMK<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||12-03-2000||03:53 PM||||First you need a new front nose. The smooth point is molded on the GT nose. The Old pieces need the end plugs or bolts removed then you push up and pull the top. Some of the holders will break. as for the nose piece there are 2 plastic studs with the stamped nuts that need to be removed from the inside. The back molding on both vehicles<BR>is molded to the rear fasica. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-03-2000||04:02 PM||||<BR>1: go on ebay and bid on a bag of the moulding clips<P>2: very carefully remove the mouldings, you can pull gently outwards on them and you might save a few of the clips BUT I DOUBT it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>3: Oreif is right, you need both new front and rear bumper covers.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>4: realize its too much work and $$ and reinstall the ribbed mouldings with the new clips you've won on E-Bay<P>Good Luck<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-03-2000||04:36 PM||||lol@2x.  i was thinkin about doing that before, but figured it would be too much trouble. once i realized i had to buy new bumpers, that idea was shot down.  my advice, forgetdaboudit  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>fiero7@hotmail.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-03-2000||06:22 PM||||Rodney Dickman also carries the side molding clips, I dont know if they are any cheaper than what you can find on ebay.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||12-03-2000||08:14 PM||||Fiero Store also has molding clips.  Also, I recently bought a quarter molding from FS; it came with clips.  Maybe all new molding kits come with clips?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||12-03-2000||11:39 PM||||  Ok Jeff, You should know by now that I get an idea in my head and there it stays untill completion. I have to replace my nose anyway and my car could use a new front facia. As for the rear, It's in good shape so maybe I could make up the difference on E-Bay. Or at least it wouldn't cost "AS" much. Then, for the rest of the moulding; There's always the old U-Pull It. This is all going to be done befor next fall when I plan on paiting the bullet. I appriciate all the info. All joking aside, It will be done, oh yeah, it will be.<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
